[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:9. A Trip to Mars]
[00:00.880] Passage 9. | 第9章。
[00:02.185] A trip to Mars. | 火星之旅。
[00:04.420] By now, a rocket will have set off on its 350 million mile trip to Mars, | 届时，一枚火箭将启程前往火星，进行其3.5亿英里的旅程，
[00:10.915] and scientists must be waiting anxiously for the results. | 科学家们一定焦急地等待着结果。
[00:14.320] The rocket will be traveling for nine months before it reaches the planet. | 火箭将飞行九个月才能到达这颗行星。
[00:18.675] It contains a number of scientific instruments, | 它包含许多科学仪器，
[00:21.560] including a television camera. | 包括一台电视摄像机。
[00:23.560] Any pictures that are taken will have to travel for three weeks before they reach the earth. | 任何拍摄到的照片都需要飞行三周才能到达地球。
[00:28.775] If the pictures are successful, | 如果照片成功，
[00:30.955] they may solve a number of problems about Mars, | 它们可能会解决关于火星的许多问题，
[00:33.725] and provide information about the markings on its surface, | 并提供关于其表面标记的信息，
[00:36.930] which nearly a hundred years ago, the astronomer Schiaparelli thought to be canals. | 几乎一百年前，天文学家斯基亚帕雷利认为这些是运河。
[00:42.150] It will be a long time before any landing on Mars can be attempted. | 任何在火星上着陆的尝试都还需要很长时间。
[00:46.590] This will only be possible when scientists have learned a lot more about the atmosphere that surrounds the planet. | 只有当科学家们对环绕这颗行星的大气层有了更多了解之后，这才会成为可能。
[00:52.485] If a satellite can one day be put into orbit around Mars, | 如果有一天能将一颗卫星送入火星轨道，
[00:56.405] scientists will be able to find out a great deal. | 科学家们将能够发现很多东西。
[00:59.705] An interesting suggestion for measuring the atmosphere around Mars has been put forward. | 一个测量火星周围大气的有趣建议被提出了。
[01:05.075] A rubber ball containing a radio transmitter could be dropped from a satellite | 一个装有无线电发射器的橡胶球可以从卫星上投放，
[01:10.115] so that it would fall towards the surface of the planet. | 这样它就会落向行星表面。
[01:13.265] The radio would signal the rate at which the ball was slowed down, | 无线电将发出信号，指示球减速的速度，
[01:17.190] and scientists would be able to calculate how dense the atmosphere is. | 科学家们将能够计算出大气的密度。
[01:21.405] It may even be possible to drop a capsule containing scientific instruments onto the planet's surface. | 甚至有可能将一个装有科学仪器的太空舱投放到行星表面。
[01:27.805] Only when a great deal more information has been obtained, | 只有当获得更多信息之后，
[01:31.310] will it be possible to plan a manned trip to Mars. | 才有可能计划载人火星之旅。